<title>POLAND: Debica 9.9-pct surge surprises traders.</title>
<headline>Debica 9.9-pct surge surprises traders.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish tyre maker Debica SA surged 9.9 percent to 83.5 zlotys in low turnover on Tuesday, a rise whose scale surprised traders.</p>
<p>Some traders said the rise might have been linked to a recent newspaper report reminding investors that the firm sought to devote its entire 36.4-million-zloty 1996 net profit to dividends.</p>
<p>Debica is 50.7-percent owned by the Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Co..</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
